## Project layout

```
src/app/
  core/       # ApiService, AuthService, interceptors, guards, models
  features/   # Feature screens (e.g. auth/login)
  shared/     # Shared UI components
  components/ # App-level components (e.g. dashboard, grid)
```

Full platform context: [early-foundations.md](docs/pharmacy_erp_architecture_docs/architecture/early-foundations.md) (Angular client layer section).

---

## HTTP and API responses

- Use [ApiService](src/app/core/services/api.service.ts) for all backend HTTP — it unwraps `{ success, data }` and throws `ApiClientError` on failure.
- Do **not** hand-parse the response envelope in components or feature services.
- Use **error codes** from `ApiClientError` for behavior — not human-readable message strings.

```typescript
// Prefer — delegate to ApiService
const response = await firstValueFrom(this.api.post<AuthTokenResponse>('/auth/login', body));

// Avoid — manual envelope handling in a component
this.http.post<ApiResponse<T>>(url, body).pipe(map(r => r.data));
```

---

## Components

- **Standalone** components with explicit `imports` array.
- Use `inject()` for DI — match existing files ([login.component.ts](src/app/features/auth/login/login.component.ts)).
- Keep components **thin**: template + form wiring + call a service; no business logic duplication.
- Use `ChangeDetectionStrategy` as existing components do (typically `OnPush` or `Eager` — match the file you edit).

---

## Services and state

- Put HTTP and session logic in `core/services/` — not in components.
- Follow existing signal usage in [AuthService](src/app/core/services/auth.service.ts): `signal`, `computed`, `asReadonly()`.
- Do **not** introduce NgRx, Akita, or other state libraries — not in this project.
- Do **not** add wrapper services around `ApiService` unless the user approves.

---

## i18n

- User-facing strings in templates via `TranslatePipe` or translate service.
- Add keys to `public/i18n/en.json` — no hardcoded UI copy in new features.

---

## Routing and guards

- Routes in [app.routes.ts](src/app/app.routes.ts).
- Use existing `authGuard` and `permissionGuard` — do not invent parallel auth checks in components.

---

## Forbidden (simplicity)

- Generic/reusable component libraries for one-off screens
- Abstract base component classes used by a single feature
- Indirection layers (facades, mediators) without a current requirement
- Highly generic pipes/directives when inline template logic is clearer

---

## Tests

- Co-locate `*.spec.ts` next to source.
- Mock `ApiService`, `AuthService`, `Router` — no real HTTP in unit tests.
- Run from repo root: `npm test`, `npm test -- --testPathPatterns=auth.service.spec`

See [testing.md](docs/pharmacy_erp_architecture_docs/architecture/testing.md) for full command reference.

